  "narrative": "Docs lead for Fernhill: billing rewrite under way; the webhooks reference waits on sd-55.\nStatus: working\n\n## Where it stands\n- Docs site: billing page rewrite under way in jx7bil3; the old plans are still live on it. (2026-09-27)\n- API reference: webhooks section regenerated from the schema; the pull request waits on sd-55. (2026-09-27)\n\n## North metric\nPages unreviewed a month after their feature shipped, from the morning staleness report (jx7stl4). Target 0.\n- 2026-08-03: 34 pages; the onboarding guides reviewed, the exports pages newly past a month\n- 2026-08-04: 34 pages; nothing cleared, the SDK changelog still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-05: 33 pages; the quickstart reviewed, the SSO guide newly past a month\n- 2026-08-06: 31 pages; the exports pages reviewed, the audit log pages newly past a month\n- 2026-08-07: 31 pages; nothing cleared, the webhooks guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-08: 31 pages; nothing cleared, the settings page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-09: 30 pages; the audit log pages reviewed, the concepts page newly past a month\n- 2026-08-10: 30 pages; nothing cleared, the quickstart still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-11: 30 pages; nothing cleared, the invite flow guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-12: 29 pages; the concepts page reviewed, the onboarding guides newly past a month\n- 2026-08-13: 29 pages; nothing cleared, the rate limits page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-14: 28 pages; the webhooks guide reviewed, the billing page newly past a month\n- 2026-08-15: 28 pages; nothing cleared, the exports pages still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-16: 28 pages; nothing cleared, the SDK changelog still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-17: 28 pages; nothing cleared, the SSO guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-18: 27 pages; the exports pages reviewed, the audit log pages newly past a month (milestone: the onboarding guides cleared)\n- 2026-08-19: 26 pages; the settings page reviewed, the webhooks guide newly past a month\n- 2026-08-20: 26 pages; nothing cleared, the settings page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-21: 26 pages; nothing cleared, the concepts page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-22: 26 pages; nothing cleared, the quickstart still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-23: 25 pages; the SDK changelog reviewed, the invite flow guide newly past a month\n- 2026-08-24: 24 pages; the concepts page reviewed, the onboarding guides newly past a month\n- 2026-08-25: 24 pages; nothing cleared, the rate limits page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-26: 23 pages; the webhooks guide reviewed, the billing page newly past a month\n- 2026-08-27: 23 pages; nothing cleared, the exports pages still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-28: 23 pages; nothing cleared, the SDK changelog still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-08-29: 21 pages; the quickstart reviewed, the SSO guide newly past a month\n- 2026-08-30: 19 pages; the exports pages reviewed, the audit log pages newly past a month\n- 2026-08-31: 18 pages; the settings page reviewed, the webhooks guide newly past a month\n- 2026-09-01: 18 pages; nothing cleared, the settings page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-02: 17 pages; the audit log pages reviewed, the concepts page newly past a month (milestone: first week under 20)\n- 2026-09-03: 16 pages; the invite flow guide reviewed, the quickstart newly past a month\n- 2026-09-04: 15 pages; the SDK changelog reviewed, the invite flow guide newly past a month\n- 2026-09-05: 15 pages; nothing cleared, the onboarding guides still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-06: 15 pages; nothing cleared, the rate limits page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-07: 15 pages; nothing cleared, the billing page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-08: 14 pages; the onboarding guides reviewed, the exports pages newly past a month\n- 2026-09-09: 14 pages; nothing cleared, the SDK changelog still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-10: 14 pages; nothing cleared, the SSO guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-11: 13 pages; the exports pages reviewed, the audit log pages newly past a month\n- 2026-09-12: 13 pages; nothing cleared, the webhooks guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-13: 12 pages; the rate limits page reviewed, the settings page newly past a month\n- 2026-09-14: 12 pages; nothing cleared, the concepts page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-15: 11 pages; the invite flow guide reviewed, the quickstart newly past a month\n- 2026-09-16: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the invite flow guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-17: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the onboarding guides still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-18: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the rate limits page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-19: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the billing page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-20: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the exports pages still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-21: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the SDK changelog still waiting on its owner (milestone: the SDK pages cleared)\n- 2026-09-22: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the SSO guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-23: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the audit log pages still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-24: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the webhooks guide still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-25: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the settings page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-26: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the concepts page still waiting on its owner\n- 2026-09-27: 11 pages; nothing cleared, the quickstart still waiting on its owner\n\n## Rules learned\n- Check a page against the running product, not against its pull request. Learned from: the plans page was approved from its diff while the live page still showed the old prices. (2026-08-14)\n- Open the live page before calling a rewrite done; a merged pull request is not a published page. Learned from: the SSO guide sat merged and unpublished for four days behind a failed deploy. (2026-08-19)\n- Verify against production, never against the diff alone. Learned from: the rate limits page matched its pull request and contradicted the API. (2026-08-27)\n- A page is reviewed when someone ran its steps, not when someone read it. Learned from: the quickstart read fine and failed at step three for every new account. (2026-08-22)\n- Run the steps of a guide on a fresh account before marking it reviewed. Learned from: the invite flow guide assumed an admin seat nobody new has. (2026-09-03)\n- Ask the feature's owner which pages a release touches before the release, not after. Learned from: the exports release changed three pages nobody had listed. (2026-08-25)\n- Get the list of touched pages from the feature owner ahead of each release. Learned from: the audit log release shipped with two stale pages. (2026-09-08)\n- Screenshots go stale first: check every image on a page when its feature changes. Learned from: the settings page text was right and its four screenshots showed the old layout. (2026-08-29)\n- Do not generate the reference from a branch; generate from the schema on main. Learned from: a reference built from a feature branch documented two endpoints that never shipped. (2026-09-01)\n- Changelog pages are written by the release owner; the docs role only links them. Learned from: a rewritten changelog entry contradicted the release notes. (2026-09-05)\n- Link checks run against the deploy preview, which needs the docs deploy token. Learned from: the link checker passed locally while three links were dead in production. (2026-09-11)\n- When two pages disagree, the one nearer the code is right until someone proves otherwise. Learned from: the concepts page was trusted over the reference and was the stale one. (2026-09-15)\n- Trust the reference over a concepts page when they conflict. Learned from: a support answer quoted the concepts page and was wrong about retries. (2026-09-19)\n- Ask the release owner for the touched pages one week ahead. Learned from: the v2 webhooks release named its pages the day it shipped. (2026-09-22)\n\n## Refuted\n- Readers leave the quickstart because it is too long: the drop is at step three, where the token step fails, at every length tested. (2026-08-23)\n- The search box returns stale pages because of the index: the index is fresh, the pages themselves were stale. (2026-08-26)\n- Support tickets about billing come from the billing page: nine of ten quoted the pricing page instead. (2026-08-31)\n- The reference generator drops deprecated fields: it keeps them; the schema had already removed them. (2026-09-04)\n- Theo's pages go stale faster than others: they are simply the pages whose features ship most often. (2026-09-09)\n- The SDK changelog needs a review cycle: nobody reads it after the first week, by the page views. (2026-09-13)\n- Broken links come from renamed pages: all but two came from the deploy preview host changing. (2026-09-17)\n- New accounts fail the quickstart because of a slow email: the token step fails with the email already delivered. (2026-08-21)\n- The reference is stale because the generator is slow to run: it runs in a minute; nobody had been asked to run it. (2026-09-02)\n\n## Standing decisions\n- Customer guides are Mara's to edit; raise a wrong guide to her and do not rewrite it. (Mara, 2026-08-12)\n- The reference is generated from the schema on main, never written or patched by hand. (Mara, 2026-08-20)\n- A page with a failing step is unpublished the same day rather than left with a warning. (Mara, 2026-08-28)\n- Screenshots are regenerated by the capture script; no hand-made image goes on a page. (Theo, 2026-09-06)\n- The docs role does not open pull requests against product code, only against the docs repo. (Mara, 2026-09-10)\n\n## Open threads\n- The onboarding guides rewrite: done, all six published and reviewed on fresh accounts. (opened 2026-08-11)\n- SSO guide stuck behind the failed deploy: closed, published 2026-08-19. (opened 2026-08-15)\n- Quickstart step three fails for new accounts: fixed and re-run on a fresh account, closed. (opened 2026-08-21)\n- Exports release pages: all three updated and closed. (opened 2026-08-24)\n- Settings screenshots: regenerated by the capture script, closed. (opened 2026-08-29)\n- Reference built from a feature branch: regenerated from main, closed. (opened 2026-09-01)\n- Audit log release pages: both updated, closed. (opened 2026-09-08)\n- Link checker needs the docs deploy token: Mara shared it on 2026-09-12, closed. (opened 2026-09-11)\n- Concepts page against the reference: concepts page corrected, closed. (opened 2026-09-15)\n- SDK changelog pages: cleared on 2026-09-21, closed. (opened 2026-09-16)\n- Rate limits page contradicted the API: corrected against production and closed. (opened 2026-08-27)\n- Invite flow guide assumed an admin seat: rewritten for a member seat, re-run on a fresh account, closed. (opened 2026-09-03)\n- Changelog entry contradicted the release notes: reverted to the release owner's words, closed. (opened 2026-09-05)\n- Search returned stale pages: the pages were refreshed and the index was never at fault, closed. (opened 2026-08-26)\n- Pricing page quoted in billing tickets: handed to Mara, who owns it; closed here. (opened 2026-08-31)\n- Deploy preview host changed and broke 14 links: 11 fixed by jx7th02, three fixed after the token arrived, closed. (opened 2026-09-17)\n- Billing page still describes the old plans; jx7bil3 is rewriting it. (opened 2026-09-24, due 2026-10-02)\n- sd-55: drop the v1 events table from the reference, or keep it marked deprecated; jx7ref2 waits on Mara. (opened 2026-09-27)\n- Six customer guides link to the v1 events table; they are Mara's to move. (opened 2026-09-27, due 2026-10-10)",
